      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Panchatantra II., 17 (Bomb. Classics) where वित्तज उष्मा (= the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "warmth of wealth,) स एव पुरुषः अर्थोष्मणा विरहितः क्षणेन अन्यः भवति इति एतत्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "विचित्रम् —Vasantatilakâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XLI.—Upajâti.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XLII.—सङ्ग the commentator explains by स्त्रीसङ्गो वा दुष्टसङ्गो वा.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "But I think the meaning is more general. It is विषयसङ्ग, attach-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "ment to worldly objects. See Bhagavadgîtâ passim. खलोपासन is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "explained by Râmarshi as दुर्जनसहचारः which is the literal mean-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "ing. It may also mean being devoted to ; संगीतोपासन occurs",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "in Mṛichchhakatika p. 6 (Calc. Ed.). One copy of the com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "mentary gives as synonymes of it सेवा and संगति. The former is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "ambiguous. अनय injustice, unfairness. त्याग giving away, liberality.",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XLIII.—Here again the language is much condensed ; वित्तस्य",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "must be supplied from the first line in the second, and तस्य must",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "be taken to answer to यो and to mean ‘his.’—Âryâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XLIV.—One copy of the commentary has एते गलितविभवा अपि",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "अर्थिषु शोभन्ते on the last line. But this is not correct, अर्थिषु गलितवि-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "भवा जनाः being co-ordinate with the other classes of persons and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "things enumerated. जनाः like मणिः and the rest is a subject of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "verb शोभन्ते. दलितो and श्यान would seem to be better readings than",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "those we have kept from C, as fitting in better with the idea of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "तनिम्ना. निहत is explained by Râmarshi in the sense of दलित viz.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "क्षत. And see Kirâta IV., 6. Why, when “मदक्षीण” the elephant",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "‘शोभते’ may be seen from Raghuvans'a IV., 23 and V., 47. About",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "rivers the commentator assigns the reason that they were पूर्वं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "महापूरेण विख्याताः. About the moon see Raghuvan'sa V., 16 and XIV.,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "80 which latter passage gives, however, a slightly different ac-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "count from that of the former. And comp. Mṛichchhakatika p.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "19 (Calc. Ed.).—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
